<h1>Tooling</h1>

<p>Pattern making and tooling design are carried out by our own tool room in Sheffield, which has supported the group since the 1960s. The team designs and builds patterns, core boxes and machining fixtures for all three sites, and maintains them for the life of each contract.</p>

<p>Keeping tooling design in-house shortens the time between a drawing change and a corrected part, since new or modified tooling does not need to be sent out to a third party. Tooling records, including revision history and storage location, are kept against the same part number used for casting and machining.</p>

<p>Tooling supports both our <a href="/products/castings">castings</a> and <a href="/products/machining">machining</a> lines. Suppliers providing raw tooling materials should refer to our <a href="/suppliers/terms">terms of supply</a>.</p>
